*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* CALL !OSDELETE(path)
*
* Deletes the operating system file PATH.  No error is reported if that fails, as the manual says; STATUS() tells.  openQM's
* statement deletes a directory too: this one deletes a file only, so that a program cannot take a directory and what is in it by
* mistake.  An ordinary program, not an internal one, as !OSREAD is: the DELETESEQ in it asks the OS-access gate of the account.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

subroutine !osdelete(path)
$catalog !osdelete

   if path = '' then return
   deleteseq path else return
   return
end

* END-CODE
